HST Office: Writer builds the ribbon only for a view of its own document.

Defensive: an abort was seen once in SfxDispatcher::QueryState while a ribbon was being built from SwDocShell::GetState
during a focus event, and its cause is not proven. With no view yet the state method fell back to SfxViewShell::Current(),
which can belong to another document. Calc and Impress already use the view of their own document only.

License: this upstream file remains under its original license (MPL-2.0).
---
--- a/sw/source/uibase/app/docsh.cxx
+++ b/sw/source/uibase/app/docsh.cxx
@@ -1123,7 +1123,9 @@
         case SID_NOTEBOOKBAR:
         {
             bool bVisible = false;
-            if (SfxViewShell* pViewShell = GetView() ? GetView() : SfxViewShell::Current())
+            SfxViewShell* pViewShell = GetView() ? GetView() : SfxViewShell::Current();
+            // not another document's view while this one is still loading (a print preview is not a SwView)
+            if (pViewShell && pViewShell->GetObjectShell() == this)
             {
                 bVisible = sfx2::SfxNotebookBar::StateMethod(pViewShell->GetViewFrame().GetBindings(),
                                                              u"modules/swriter/ui/");
